      "Figure 13.1 Demarcation of the Periodic Table.",
      "In previous grades, you have learnt about the periodic classification of elements in groups and periods. You have also learnt the basics about the 1\", 2\" period elements. In this unit you will study more detail about the periodic trends and some properties of period (Na to Ar), Groups IA, IIA, IVA and VIIA elements.",
      "2",
      "*",
      "13.1 Period 3 (Na To Ar)",
      "NOT FOR SALE",
      "Period 3 elements consists of sodium (Na), magnesium (Mg), aluminium (Al), silicon (Si), phosphorous (P), sulphur (S), chlorine (CI) and argon (Ar). Sodium and magnesium are metals and belong to s-block. Aluminum (metal), silicon (metalloid), phosphorus, sulphur, chlorine and argon are non-metals and belong to p-block.",
      "13.1.1 Physical and Atomic Properties of the Elements",
      "The properties of the atoms of the elements are called atomic properties. On moving from. left to right, in a period and from top to bottom, in a group of the periodic table, atomic properties show a regular variations. Hence, these properties, are also called periodic properties. Certain important periodic and physical properties of period 3 elements have been discussed in this unit.",
      "13.1.1.1 Electronic Structure",
      "In third period of the periodic table electrons are successively filled in 3s and 3p orbital of atoms of elements (Na to Ar). The electronic configurations of these elements are given below where [Ne] represents the electronic configuration of neon.",
      "Table 13.1 Elements, their Symbols and electronic configurations.",
