      "As we move in a period from left to right, the number of shells remains the same as the electrons are added in the same shell. However, the effective nuclear charge increases and pulls the electron cloud closer to the nucleus. As a result, the atomic size decreases from sodium (Na) to chlorine (CI) in period third.",
