      "0 0",
      "Sodium, magnesium and aluminium are all metals and are good conductors of electricity. These metals conduct electricity because they contain free electrons. Going from sodium to aluminium, the number of free electrons increases and thus the electrical conductivity increases. Silicon has a giant covalent structure. It is a semiconductor, so it is not a good. conductor. Phosphorus, sulphur, chlorine and argon are non-conductor as they are non-metals. 13.1.1.6 Trend in Melting and Boiling Points",
