      "NOT FOR SALE",
      "Key Points",
      "Group - IA and Group - IIA elements belong to s-block. Group-IVA and Group - VIIA elements belong to p-block. Atomic radius of all the groups increases down the group.",
      "Period 3\" consists of metals (Na, Mg and Al), metalloid (Si) and non-metals (P, S, CI and Ar).",
      "Atomic radius decreases in period 3 up to chlorine but argon does not follow this trend. All the elements of period 3\" react with oxygen and form the oxides, except argon. Period 3\" oxides do not conduct electricity in solid state.",
      "The chlorides of period 3\" i.e. NaCl, MgCl, and Al,Cl, are in solid state, while the SiCl,, PCI, and S,Cl, are in liquid state.",
      "Density of Group - IA elements increases down the group.",
      "Normal oxides of Group - IA on reaction with dilute acids produce salts and water. The carbonates of Group - IA do not decompose on heating except lithium carbonate. Group – IA metals give characteristics colours to the Bunsen flame. Beryllium is the only alkaline earth metal, which does not react with water even at red heat.",
      "Be, Mg and Ca on reaction with oxygen form normal oxides.",
      "Sr and Ba react with oxygen and form peroxide.",
      "BeO are amphoteric whereas other oxides of Group - IIA metals are strong bases. Inert pair effect is the non-participation of the two 's' electrons in bonding. In CO2 molecule, carbon atom is sp and each oxygen atom is sp2 hybridized. Silicon dioxide is weakly acidic.",
      "Electron affinity is the amount of energy released when an electron is added to an isolated gaseous atom to form an anion.",
      "In Group-VIIA the electron affinity generally decreases in the order (I<Br<F<CI). In Group-VIIA the order of decreasing power as oxidizing agent is F, >Cl, Br, >I.",
      "C C C C",
