      "72stha NOT FOR SALE Transition metals have variable oxidation states and hence are capable of forming",
      "+ Ivers intermediate compounds, which help in the formation of desired product. For example, finely divided iron is used as a catalyst in Haber's process for the synthesis of ammonia, while V2O, is used in the conversion of SO2 to SO3 for the manufacture of H2SO, by contact process. TiCl4 is used in the polymerization of ethene to polythene polymer.",
      "The application of nickel (Ni), palladium (Pd) or platinum (Pt) in the catalytic hydrogenation of unsaturated hydrocarbons and the use of copper (Cu) in the oxidation of ethanol to acetaldehyde are example of catalytic properties of transition elements. 2F a2 + $2082 - (y) 2502 + 2 Festo",
      "14.1.6Magnetic Behaviour",
      "Substances show two different types of behaviours when subjected to an external magnetic field. If a substance is weakly attracted by a strong magnetic field, it is called paramagnetic substance, whereas a substance weakly repelled by magnetic field is called diamagnetic substance.",
      "Paramagnetic behaviour of a substance is due to interaction of magnetic field produced by spinning of one or more unpaired electrons in an atom, ion or molecule with external magnetic field.",
      "In diamagnetic substances the electrons are paired up due to which magnetic field of oppositely spinning electrons cancel each other.",
      "Metals like Fe, Co and Ni possess very high paramagnetic nature and attain permanent magnetic moment hence, they are ferromagnetic as shown by Fe and Mn2+ ions which have five unpaired electrons each.",
      "14.1.7 Alloy Formation 4 mixture containing two or more metallic Elements metallic and nonmetallic elements",
      "An alloy is a mixture of a metal with another element, either métal or non-metal.",
      "usually fused together Transition metals have another great characteristic that they easily mix with each other. This is because all the d-block metals have similarity in their atomic sizes. Some transition metal atoms allow to replace easily in crystal lattice.",
      "An alloy in which one of the components is mercury is known as amalgam. In alloys the chemical properties of the component elements are retained but certain physical properties are improved. Alloys are more shiny, stronger and harder than the pure metal. They are rigid, light weight, durable, thermally more stable, less reactive and corrosion resistant as compared to its component elements.",
