      "NOT FOR SALE",
      "the colour complementary to that of the absorbed light. The colour of the transmitted light is different from the colour of the absorbed light and is known as the complementary colour of the absorbed light. The colour of the transition metal complex is the colour of this transmitted light.",
      "If the complex absorbs all colours except orange, the complex appears orange. The complex will also appear orange if it absorbs only light of the colour blue. In a complementary manner, if the complex ion absorbed only orange, it would appear blue. Blue and orange are referred to as complementary colours. In [Ti(H2O)], yellow and green lights are absorbed, while most of the blue and red lights are transmitted, therefore the solution of [Ti(H2O)<]* ions looks purple in colour.",
