      "Manganese is the third most abundant transition metal after iron and titanium. Manganese, (Mn), is silvery white, brittle metallic element used principally in making alloys. The atomic number of manganese is 25 and atomic mass 54.938 a.m.u.",
      "14.3.3.1 Oxidation States",
      "According to the electronic configuration of manganese (3d3, 4s2), it shows a maximum oxidation state of +7. In addition to this state, it also shows lower oxidation states such as +6, +4, +3 and +2.",
      "Manganese compounds in which \"Mn' is in +7 oxidation state, are restricted to the unstable oxide Mn,O, and compounds of intensely purple permanganate ion (MnO4) and are powerful oxidizing agents. Mno* is present in MnO, in the salt of manganic acid (H,MnO,). The free acid is unknown. Its salts are called manganates e.g. KMnO4-",
      "The compounds having Mn\" are very limited in number. The most familiar",
      "compound of Mn** is MnO,.",
      "68",
