      "The compound of Mn3 is called manganic compound. In aqueous solution Mn+ ions is quite unstable since it is easily reduced to Mn2+ ions e.g. H.Mn,O,, Mn,(SO),.",
      "Mn+ le",
      "Mn2+",
      "+2 is the most stable oxidation state of Mn in neutral or acidic solution. Mn2+ ion exists as pale pink hexaaquamanganese(II) [Mn(H,O),], which is quite stable to oxidation. The stability of Mn2+ is due to half-filled 3d orbital.",
      "The compounds of Mn2+ are called manganous compounds such as MnO, MnCO,, MnSO.. MnCl, etc.",
      "14.3.3.2 Potassium Manganate (VII) as an Oxidizing Agent in Organic Chemistry Potassium manganate (VII) is a powerful oxidizing agent. It is usually used in neutral or alkaline solution in organic chemistry. Acidified potassium manganate (VII) tends to be destructively strong oxidizing agent, breaking carbon-carbon bonds. The potassium manganate (VII) solution is usually made mildly alkaline with sodium carbonate solution and the typical colour changes are:",
