        "theory": "a. Anthracite b. Lignite 4. Petroleum is mainly a mixture of a. heterocyclic compounds. c. saturated hydrocarbons.\nc. sugar\nc. methane\npercentage of carbon is\nc. Peat\n5. The major component of natural gas is\na. butane\nb. ethane\nd. alcohol\nd. acetic acid\nd. Bituminous\nb. aromatic Hydrocarbons. d. unsaturated hydrocarbons.\nd. methane\nc. propane\nby destructive distillation of coal except c. coal gas.\nd. coke.\n6. All of the following fractions are obtained\na. coal tar.\nb. refinery gas.\n7. Coal can be converted to petroleum by\na. Haber process.\nc. Fischer-Tropsch process.\nb. Destructive distillation.\n8. Pyridine belongs to which class of organic compounds\na. heterocyclic\nc. alicyclic\nd. Fractional distillation.\nb. hydrocarbon\nd. homocyclic\n9. Which of the following represents the functional group of amides?\nb. -NH2\nc. -C=N\na. -COOR 10. Which of the following elements can not be detected in a given organic compound, directly?\na. Chlorine b. Phosphorous c. Nitrogen\n11. Lassaigne&#x27;s solution is used to test the presence of\na. nitrogen. b. halogen.\nc. sulphur.\nd. -CONH2\nd. Oxygen\nd. all of these.\n12. Lassigne&#x27;s solution plus silver nitrate gives yellow precipitate which is insoluble\nin ammonium hydroxide. This shows the presence of\na. nitrogen b. sulphur\nc. iodine\n13. Fischer-Tropsch synthesis involve the formation of alkanes by the combination of\na. CO and H2 b. CO2 and H2\nc. C and H2\n14. Bucky balls consists of.......... carbon rings\na. tetragonal\nb. pentagonal\n97\nc. hexagonal\nd. carbon\nd. All of these\nd. b and c both.\nX\n15. Pyridine\na. is homocyclic compound.\nc. is heterocyclic compound.\nNOT FOR SALE\nb. contains nitrogen.\nd. both b and c.\nQ2. Write short answers of the following questions.\ni.\n11.\niii.\nWhat is meant by organic compounds and organic chemistry?\nWrite down the procedure for the test of presence of nitrogen in organic compound.\nWhat is homologous series? Give the characteristics of homologous series. iv. Although bucky ball is an allotropic form of carbon, but it is included in\norganic chemistry.\nMention those compounds which although contain carbon but are not considered organic.\nvi. Differentiate between partial and total synthesis?\nvii. How coal can be converted into petroleum?\nviii. Discuss the reasons for the presence of large number of organic compounds? ix. Differentiate between acyclic and cyclic organic compounds.\nQ3. Write detail answers of the following questions.\n1. What are fossil fuels? Discuss different types of fossil fuels.\n2. Elaborate the detection of various elements in organic compound.\n3. Write the different fractions obtained by the destructive distillation of coal. Give\ntheir importance.\n4. Explain some of the important characteristics of organic compounds.",
        "content": "a. Anthracite b. Lignite 4. Petroleum is mainly a mixture of a. heterocyclic compounds. c. saturated hydrocarbons.<br>c. sugar<br>c. methane<br>percentage of carbon is<br>c. Peat<br>5. The major component of natural gas is<br>a. butane<br>b. ethane<br>d. alcohol<br>d. acetic acid<br>d. Bituminous<br>b. aromatic Hydrocarbons. d. unsaturated hydrocarbons.<br>d. methane<br>c. propane<br>by destructive distillation of coal except c. coal gas.<br>d. coke.<br>6. All of the following fractions are obtained<br>a. coal tar.<br>b. refinery gas.<br>7. Coal can be converted to petroleum by<br>a. Haber process.<br>c. Fischer-Tropsch process.<br>b. Destructive distillation.<br>8. Pyridine belongs to which class of organic compounds<br>a. heterocyclic<br>c. alicyclic<br>d. Fractional distillation.<br>b. hydrocarbon<br>d. homocyclic<br>9. Which of the following represents the functional group of amides?<br>b. -NH2<br>c. -C=N<br>a. -COOR 10. Which of the following elements can not be detected in a given organic compound, directly?<br>a. Chlorine b. Phosphorous c. Nitrogen<br>11. Lassaigne&#x27;s solution is used to test the presence of<br>a. nitrogen. b. halogen.<br>c. sulphur.<br>d. -CONH2<br>d. Oxygen<br>d. all of these.<br>12. Lassigne&#x27;s solution plus silver nitrate gives yellow precipitate which is insoluble<br>in ammonium hydroxide. This shows the presence of<br>a. nitrogen b. sulphur<br>c. iodine<br>13. Fischer-Tropsch synthesis involve the formation of alkanes by the combination of<br>a. CO and H2 b. CO2 and H2<br>c. C and H2<br>14. Bucky balls consists of.......... carbon rings<br>a. tetragonal<br>b. pentagonal<br>97<br>c. hexagonal<br>d. carbon<br>d. All of these<br>d. b and c both.<br>X<br>15. Pyridine<br>a. is homocyclic compound.<br>c. is heterocyclic compound.<br>NOT FOR SALE<br>b. contains nitrogen.<br>d. both b and c.<br>Q2. Write short answers of the following questions.<br>i.<br>11.<br>iii.<br>What is meant by organic compounds and organic chemistry?<br>Write down the procedure for the test of presence of nitrogen in organic compound.<br>What is homologous series? Give the characteristics of homologous series. iv. Although bucky ball is an allotropic form of carbon, but it is included in<br>organic chemistry.<br>Mention those compounds which although contain carbon but are not considered organic.<br>vi. Differentiate between partial and total synthesis?<br>vii. How coal can be converted into petroleum?<br>viii. Discuss the reasons for the presence of large number of organic compounds? ix. Differentiate between acyclic and cyclic organic compounds.<br>Q3. Write detail answers of the following questions.<br>1. What are fossil fuels? Discuss different types of fossil fuels.<br>2. Elaborate the detection of various elements in organic compound.<br>3. Write the different fractions obtained by the destructive distillation of coal. Give<br>their importance.<br>4. Explain some of the important characteristics of organic compounds.",
