      "propanone",
      "(keto form)",
      "он",
      "CH2=C−CH3",
      "propen-2-ol (enol form)",
      "The result of this keto-enol tautomerization, is the migration of a proton from one location to another, accompanied by a change in location of the pi bond.",
      "126",
      "*",
      "16.6.2",
      "Stereoisomerism",
      "NOT FOR SALE",
      "When isomerism is caused by different arrangement of atoms or groups. phenomenon is called stereoisomerism. Thus, the stereoisomers have the same in space, the molecular formula and connectivity of atoms, but differ in the arrangement of atoms or groups in",
      "space. In other words, the isomers that have the same constitution but differ in the spatial arrangement of their atoms are called stereoisomers. Some stereoisomers which are inter-convertible by rotation of single bond are called conformational isomers. But the stereoisomers which are not inter-convertible without breaking and making of some bonds, are called configurational isomers. Conformational isomerism is beyond the scope of this book, so we will discuss only the configurational isomerism in stereoisomers, which is of two types i.e. geometric and optical isomerism. 16.6.2.1 Geometrical Isomerism",
      "Geometric isomers have different arrangement of atoms or groups when the rotation is restricted in a molecule. For example, but-2-ene have two stereoisomeric forms, cis-but-2-ene and trans-but-2-ene, as shown below.",
      "ilab.com",
      "H",
      "C:",
      "C",
      "cis-but-2-ene",
      "CH,",
