      "17.1.2 Structure of Alkyl Halides",
      "NOT FOR SALE",
      "To understand the structure of alkyl halides, let us consider methyl chloride as an xample. In this molecule the carbon atom is sp'-hybridized and all the bonds of carbon re sigma. During the process of bond formation, one sp-hybrid orbital of carbon atom verlaps with the half-filled p orbital of chlorine atom and form carbon-chlorine sigma wond, while the remaining three sp'-hybrid orbitals overlap with Is orbitals of three ydrogen atoms and form three carbon-hydrogen sigma bonds (Figure 17.1). The bond engths of carbon-chlorine and carbon-hydrogen bonds are 178 pm and 108 pm espectively. The H-C-H and H-C-Cl bond angles are approximately equal to 109.5°.",
