        "id": "18.16",
        "title": "Textbook lesson extract 15",
        "theory": "General formula of ether is R-O-R.\nEthers react with cold conc. HCl or H2SO, to form oxonium salt.\nIn Williamson synthesis method, sodium alkoxide is treated with an alkyl halide to produce ether.\nHydrogen bonding in alcohols result in relatively high boiling points and good miscibility with water.\nCCC\n221\nNOT FOR SALE\nExercise\nQI. Choose the correct one from the given options.\n1. Isopropyl alcohol is a type of\na. primary alcohol.\nc. tertiary alcohol.\nb. secondary alcohol.\nd. none of these.\n2. Which of the following has the highest boiling point?\na. Dimethyl ether\nc. n-propyl alcohol\n3. Trimethylene glycol is a\na. vic-diol.\nc. triol.\nb. Ethyl alcohol\nd. Isopropyl alcohol\nb. gem-diol.\nd. none of these.\nThe final product of oxidative cleavage of ethylene glycol with periodic acid is\na. formaldehyde.\nc. formic acid.\nb. acetaldehyde.\nd.\nmixture of formaldehyde and acetaldehyde.\n5. Oxygen carrying positive charge and bonded to three other atoms is called\na. oxide ion.\nc. carbocation.\nb. oxonium ion.\nd. carbanion.\n6. Which of the proper reagent used for oxidation of a primary alcohol to aldehyde?\na. Acidified dichromate\nc. Acidified permanganate\n7. Which one is an aromatic alcohol?\na. methyl alcohol\nb. Acidified chromate\nd. PCC\nb. ethyl alcohol\nd. p-cresol\n8. Compound which is added to natural gas to make gas leakage detectable?\nc. benzyl alcohol\na. phenol\nc. methanol\nb. ethanthiol\nd. hydrogen sulphide\nb. ethanol\n9. Which of the following is more reactive toward Lucas Reagent?\na. methanol\nc. 2-methyl-2-propanol\nd. 2-butanol\n10. Ethoxyethane when treated with conc. H2SO, produces.\na. carbocation\nc. carbanion\nb. oxonium ion\nd. oxalate ion\n222\n11. Lucas Reagent is\na. Zn-Hg/HCI\nc. Zn +H2O\nNOT FOR SALE\nb. ZnCl2 + HCl\nd. Na+ liq.NH,\n12. The reaction of an alcohol with sodium produces\na. ethane\nc. alkoxide\nb. ethene\nd. aldehyde\n13. Benzene diazonium salt is a reactive salt and upon hydrolysis yields\na. phenol.\nc. diazobenzene.\n14. Oxidation of secondary alcohol gives\na. carboxylic acid\nc. aldehyde\nb. benzene.\nd. benzoic acid.",
