        "title": "Textbook lesson extract 7",
        "theory": "The reaction is catalyzed by an acid. The mechanism is similar to general acid-catalysed\nmechanism discussed in Section 19.6.1.\n0:\nडिप\nIdehyde/ketone oxonium ion\nOH\nOH,\nNH2X\n-C-\n+ H2O\n-H+\n-H+\nXN-H\ncondensation\naddition product\nNHX\neactions of ammonia and ammonia derivatives are given below.\nproduct\n¥\n239\n*\nH\n401\n0\nH\nC- aldehyde/ketone\n+ H-N-H\nC\n+ H2O\nimine\nammonia\nR\nN\nH\nC- + H-N-R\nC- + H2O\nN-substituted imine\naldehyde/ketone\n1o-amine\n(sec-imine)\nOH\nN\nH\nH+\naldehyde/ketone\nC- +H-N-OH\nhydroxylamine\nC-\noxime\n+ H2O\nNH2\nH\nCH2O\n+ H−NNH,\naldehyde/ketone\nhydrazine\n0\nH\nhydrazone\nNH−CH,\nH*\n-C+H2O\nphenyl hydrazine\nphenyl hydrazone\nC- + H−N-NH—CH,\naldehyde/ketone\n19.6.3.5 Using Oxygen Nucleophiles\nWater and alcohols are oxygen nucleophiles. They can add to carbonyl group to for\naddition products.\na. Using Water\naw\nWhen aldehydes or ketones react with water, they add a water molecule and for geminal diols (1,1-diols). The reaction is called hydration and can be catalyzed by acid\nor any hydroxide base.\nOH\n-c-\nHor OH\n+ H-OH\n-C-\naldehyde/ketone\nwater",
        "content": "The reaction is catalyzed by an acid. The mechanism is similar to general acid-catalysed<br>mechanism discussed in Section 19.6.1.<br>0:<br>डिप<br>Idehyde/ketone oxonium ion<br>OH<br>OH,<br>NH2X<br>-C-<br>+ H2O<br>-H+<br>-H+<br>XN-H<br>condensation<br>addition product<br>NHX<br>eactions of ammonia and ammonia derivatives are given below.<br>product<br>¥<br>239<br>*<br>H<br>401<br>0<br>H<br>C- aldehyde/ketone<br>+ H-N-H<br>C<br>+ H2O<br>imine<br>ammonia<br>R<br>N<br>H<br>C- + H-N-R<br>C- + H2O<br>N-substituted imine<br>aldehyde/ketone<br>1o-amine<br>(sec-imine)<br>OH<br>N<br>H<br>H+<br>aldehyde/ketone<br>C- +H-N-OH<br>hydroxylamine<br>C-<br>oxime<br>+ H2O<br>NH2<br>H<br>CH2O<br>+ H−NNH,<br>aldehyde/ketone<br>hydrazine<br>0<br>H<br>hydrazone<br>NH−CH,<br>H*<br>-C+H2O<br>phenyl hydrazine<br>phenyl hydrazone<br>C- + H−N-NH—CH,<br>aldehyde/ketone<br>19.6.3.5 Using Oxygen Nucleophiles<br>Water and alcohols are oxygen nucleophiles. They can add to carbonyl group to for<br>addition products.<br>a. Using Water<br>aw<br>When aldehydes or ketones react with water, they add a water molecule and for geminal diols (1,1-diols). The reaction is called hydration and can be catalyzed by acid<br>or any hydroxide base.<br>OH<br>-c-<br>Hor OH<br>+ H-OH<br>-C-<br>aldehyde/ketone<br>water",
        "rules": [],
        "sciNote": "The reaction is catalyzed by an acid. The mechanism is similar to general acid-catalysed\nmechanism discussed in Section 19.6.1.\n0:\nडिप\nIdehyde/ketone oxonium ion\nOH\nOH,\nNH2X\n-C-\n+ H2O\n-H+\n-H+\nXN-H\ncondensation\naddition product\nNHX\neactions of ammonia and ammonia derivatives are given below.\nproduct\n¥\n239\n*\nH\n401\n0\nH\nC- aldehyde/ketone\n+ H-N-H\nC\n+ H2O\nimine\nammonia\nR\nN\nH\nC- + H-N-R\nC- + H2O\nN-substituted imine\naldehyde/ketone\n1o-amine\n(sec-imine)\nOH\nN\nH\nH+\naldehyde/ketone\nC- +H-N-OH\nhydroxylamine\nC-\noxime\n+ H2O\nNH2\nH\nCH2O\n+ H−NNH,\naldehyde/ketone\nhydrazine\n0\nH\nhydrazone\nNH−CH,\nH*\n-C+H2O\nphenyl hydrazine\nphenyl hydrazone\nC- + H−N-NH—CH,\naldehyde/ketone\n19.6.3.5 Using Oxygen Nucleophiles\nWater and alcohols are oxygen nucleophiles. They can add to carbonyl group to for\naddition products.\na. Using Water\naw\nWhen aldehydes or ketones react with water, they add a water molecule and for geminal diols (1,1-diols). The reaction is called hydration and can be catalyzed by acid\nor any hydroxide base.\nOH\n-c-\nHor OH\n+ H-OH\n-C-\naldehyde/ketone\nwater"
