      "Isomerism in Aldehydes and Ketones",
      "phenylethanone",
      "(acetophenone)",
      "Aldehydes containing four or more carbon atoms and ketones containing five or more carbon atoms can exhibit chain isomerism. For example, butanal and 2-methylpropanal are chain isomers of aldehydes containing four carbon atoms, while pentan-2-one and 3-methylbutanone are chain isomers of ketone containing five carbon atoms. Ketones having five or more carbon atoms and aromatic aldehydes can exhibit position isomerism. For example, pentan-2-one and pentan-3-one are position isomers of ketone having five carbon atoms. Aromatic aldehydes can also show position isomerism e.g. benzene-1,2-dicarbaldehyde, benzene-1,3-dicarbaldehyde and benzene-1,4- dicarbaldehyde are position isomers.",
      "CHO",
