      "19.6.2",
      "Relative Reactivity",
      "Generally aldehydes are more reactive than ketones towards nucleophilic additions, They usually react more quickly than ketones and the position of the equilibrium usually lies more toward the products than with ketones. The enhanced reactivity of",
      "aldehydes is due to an electronic effect and a steric effect.",
      "(a) Electronic Effect",
