        "sciNote": "Carbonyl Compounds 2: Carboxylic Acids and Functional Derivatives\nTeaching\n7\nAssessment\nWeightage %\n6\nAfter studying this unit, students will be able to:\nDescribe preparation of carboxylic acids by carbonation of Grignard's Reagent, hydrolysis of nitriles, oxidation of primary alcohols, oxidation of aldehydes and oxidation of alkyl benzene. (Applying)\nDiscuss reactivity of carboxylic acids. (Applying)\nDescribe the chemistry of carboxylic acids by conversion to carboxylic acid derivatives i.e. acyl halides, acid anhydrides, esters, amides and reactions involving inter conversion of these. (Analyzing)\nDescribe reactions of carboxylic acid derivatives. (Applying)\nDescribe isomerism in carboxylic acids. (Understanding)\n:0:\nR-C-Ci:\nacid chloride\n:0:\nR-C-O:\ncarboxylate\nR\n10:\n10:\nΠ\nacid anhydride\n:0:\nΠ\nR-C-OH\n:0:\nester\n249\nR-C=N:\nnitrile\n:0:\nH\nR-C-N\nH\namide\nIntroduction\nNOT FOR SALE\nThe combination of a carbonyl group and a hydroxyl is called a carboxyl group; carb. from carbonyl and-oxyl from hydroxyl. Compounds containing the carboxyl group are\ndistinctly acidic and are called carboxylic acids.\n0\nC-O-H carboxyl group\nCarboxylic acids may be aliphatic or aromatic depending upon whether carboxyl group is attached to an alkyl group or an aryl group. The simplest acid is formic acid (HCOOH), with a hydrogen atom bonded to the carboxyl group, and also an aliphatic acid. Fatty acids are long-chain aliphatic carboxylic acids derived from the hydrolysis of fats and oils. Acids containing ",
        "diagramSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Carbonyl Compounds II: Carboxylic Acids and Functional Derivatives\" style=\"width:min(100%,460px);height:auto;background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbeafe;border-radius:10px;margin:12px 0\"><text x=\"85\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"18\">R—C(=O)—OH</text><path d=\"M220 103H260\" stroke=\"#059669\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M250 93L260 103L250 113\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#059669\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"273\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"17\">ester / amide</text><text x=\"155\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"14\">carboxyl derivatives</text></svg>",
