        "sciNote": "NMgX R-C-R\ngrignard reagent\nH2O*\n(workup)\nR-C-R\nnitrile\nimine salt\nketone\n1. CH,MgBr\nCH, CEN\nCH,-C-CH,\n2. H,0*\nmethanenitrile\n20.7.5\nacetone\nSummary of the Reactions that Interconvert Carboxylic Acid\nDerivatives\nA summary of the reactions of different derivatives of carboxylic acids with certain nucleophiles, have been listed in Table 20.5.\nThe different acids derivatives are listed at the left of the chart in order of decreasing reactivities towards nucleophiles. The common nucleophiles are listed across the top. In case of hydrolysis, corresponding acid is obtained, we either start with an acyl\n265\nNOT FOR SA\nhalides, acid anhydride, ester, amide or nitrile. Similarly alcoholysis gives an ester ammonolysis gives an amide. All of the reactions in Table 20.5 take place via atta the nucleophile on the carbonyl carbon of the acid derivative, commonly c\nnucleophilic acyl substitution.\nTable 20.5\nAcid derivative\nReactions of Acid Derivatives with certain Derivatives Nucleophile\nH2O\n(Hydrolysis)\nReaction of acid derivatives with\nROH (Alcoholysis)\nNH\n(Ammonolysis\n8\nR-C-C\nacid halide\ni i\nR-C-0-C-R\nanhydride\ni\nR-C-OR\nester\n0\nR-C-OH + HCL\ncarboxylic acid\nO\n2R-C-OH\ncarboxylic acid\nR-C-OH + ROH\ncarboxylic acid alcohol\nester\nR-C-OR+HCI\nR−C−NH_ + HC\namide\n0\nR—C—NH2+R—C-\ncarboxylic acid\namide\ncarboxyl\nO\ni\nester\nR-C-OR+R-C-OH\nR-C-OR + ROH\nester\nR-C-NH, R\nalcohol\namide\nR-C-NH\nR-C-OH+NH2\namide\ncarboxylic acid\nR-CEN\nnitrile\nR-C-OH+NH2\ncarboxylic acid\nawaze in\nalce\nSelf-assessinet\nWrite the com",
