      "on groups structure of the enzyme.",
      "Each enzyme has a pH at which it shows the maximum activity. This pH is called optimum pH. For example, the optimum pH of pepsin is around 2.0 while that of trypsin varies from 8-9 pH. The pH below which the enzyme loses its activity and at which the enzymes shows the lowest activity is called minimum pH. Most of the enzymes have optimum",
