      "21.3.3 Industrial Application of Enzymes",
      "Enzymes are used in the chemical industry and other industrial applications where",
      "extremely specific catalysts are required.",
      "Useful enzymes are obtained from both plants and animals, but most enzymes are obtained from microorganism, mainly bacteria and fungi. Some applications of enzymes are given below.",
      "i.",
      "Biological detergents",
      "Most of the enzymes for washing come from bacteria adapted to live in hot springs. The enzymes are used for presoak condition and direct liquid applications helping removal of proteins and starch stains. They are also able to digests fat, oil and",
      "ii.",
      "Fruit juice production",
      "During the manufacture of fruit juice, the cells of the fruits have to be broken down before the bulk of the juice can be extracted. Plant cell wall is built of cellulose fibers, which are held together by pectins and hemicelluloses and they are extremely tough. When very high temperature is used to break down the fruit tissues, this will",
      "Tidbit",
      "Cellulases",
      "grease stains.",
      "Cellulases is an enzyme that breaks down the cellulose molecule into monosaccharaides \"simple sugars\". The breakdown of cellulose is on considerable economic importance.",
      "affect colour and flavour of the juice. Instead, the fruit is crushed and enzyme preparation containing cellulases and hemicellulases are added. These cause cell wall to break up most of the juice is released.",
      "iii.",
      "Production of ethanol",
      "In biological industry, cellulase are used to break down cellulose into sugar which can then be fermented to produce ethanol.",
      "iv. High fructose syrup",
      "A sweetener that is widely used in food and drinks is high fructose corn syrup. It is manufactured from starch in corn fruit. The grains are milled to starch slurry and the enzyme amylase is added. Finally, the syrup is passed down a column of immobilized glucose isomerase enzymes. This converts much of glucose to fructose. It is added",
      "sweeten foods without adding too many calories.",
      "290",
      "NOT FOR SALE",
      "industry, enzymes like amylases, xylanases and cellulases etc. are used. Beside this, numerous enzymes are used in other industrial processes; such as, in paper",
      "21.4 Lipids",
