        "sciNote": "Nail polish should have proper viscosity, gloss and drying properties. It should be harmless to skin and convenient to apply.\nNail varnish or nail polish is a lacquer applied to human finger nails or toe nails usually cosmetically but also as protection for the nails. Nail polish started traditionally in clear red, pink and brown colour. With passage of time, many new colours and techniques have been developed. Beyond solid colours, nail polish has also developed an array of other designs and colour, such as nail polish stamps, crackled, magnetic nail polish strips and stickers.\nUses of Nail Polishes\nClish strips\nNail polishes are used for decoration but also to cause nail growth, make nails stronger, prevent nails from breaking, oracking and slitting and to stop nail biting. Nail polishes are used to restore moisture to the nail and help polish adhere to the nail. It extends the lifespan of the manicure.\nComposition of Nail Polish\nThere is no single formula for nail polish. There are a number of ingredients that are used in nail polish preparation. The basic components include film forming agents,\nresins and plasticizers, solvents and colouring agent.\n324\nLacquer Base\nNOT FOR SALE\nFilm former: Nail polishes are made up of nitrocellulose dissolved in a solvent (e.g. butyl acetate or ethyl acetate). It forms a thin film on the nail after application. This film is hard and water-proof and abrasion resistance. Adhesive polymers (e.g. Tosylamide /formaldehyde resin) are added to "
