      "Synthetic Polymers (PVC and Nylon)",
      "A polymer is a macromolecule (sometimes with a very high molecular weight) formed as a result of",
      "Tidbit",
      "a process known as polymerization, whereby Difference between Polymer",
      "small organic molecules combine together to form large molecules (polymers).",
      "The small molecules, which undergo polymerization, are called 'the monomers'. Thus, a polymer is a large molecule built up from many hundreds or thousands of monomer units joined together.",
      "A synthetic compound is man-made and produced",
      "as a result of chemical reactions. A synthetic polymer is a man-made macromolecule that is made of thousands of repeating units.",
      "and Macromolecules Polymers are also calle macromolecules due to their larg size but converse is not alway true. A macromolecule may may not contain monomer unit e.g., chlorophyll (C,H2O,N‚Mg is a macromolecule but not",
      "polymer since there are m",
      "monomer units present so we ca conclude that all polymers an macromolecules while macromolecules may not B polymers in nature.",
      "The well-known synthetic polymer is plastic polyethylene or polythene which is composed of large molecules formed by the repeated combination of ethene molecules. Polyn are classified as either 'addition polymers' or 'condensation polymers' depending",
      "their method of formation.",
      "1. Addition Polymers",
      "The polymers formed by the polymerization of monomers containing double or tri bonds (unsaturated compounds) are called addition polymers. Thus, addition polyn results from the self- combination of many monomer units into a substance wit molecular weight which is a multiple of the monomer.",
      "H",
