        "sciNote": "vii. Out of CFCs and CO2 which one has higher potential to cause global warmin\nand why?\nviii. Why does the rain water normally have pH of about 5.6 and when does it chan\ninto acid rain?\nix. Which gases are converted to harmless gases by 3-way catalytic converter?\nQ3. Write detail answers of the following questions.\n1.\n(i) Green Chemistry is a new route to the protection of environment'. Comm\non it.\n356\n*\n2.\n3.\n4.\n5.\nNOT FOR SALE\n(ii) What is greenhouse effect? How is it causing global warming?\nWhat is meant by atmosphere? Explain the various layers of atmosphere. (ii) Define air pollution and discuss its effects.\n(1) What is role of ozone layer in upper atmosphere?\n(ii) What will happen if ozone is no more present in upper atmosphere? What is water pollution? What are the main sources of water pollution? Write note on the following.\n(a) Acid rain\n(c) Water treatment\nProject\nTo build a water filtration apparatus.\n(b) Smog\n(d) Chemistry of stratosphere\nTake a soft drink plastic bottle, cut it in the middle leaving the lower part a little longer than the upper one. The upper part will be used as funnel and the lower part as receiving part. Put some cotton at the mouth of the bottle as a plug and some sand above the cotton plug. (the sand must be washed and dried beforehand so as to remove any dust or water-soluble substances). Put this funnel in the receiving part and add some muddy water slowly in it. You will see the filtered water as clean and transparent as the fresh water.\n"
