        "theory": "391\nNOT FOR SALE\nSubstituent group: A substituent is an atom or group of atoms which replaces one or more hydrogen or other atom or group of atoms on the parent molecule.\nSubstrate: It is a molecule or a compound that undergoes a chemical reaction, whether under the action of a catalyst, an enzyme or an inhibitor. It can also refer to a surface on which other chemical reactions are performed.\nSulphydryl or Marcapto: A mercapto group is a functional group containing a sulfur atom bonded to a hydrogen atom. General formula: -SH.\nSynthetic Organic Compound: The compounds which can be synthesized laboratory by chemical manipulations (chemical reactions) from living or non-living\norganisms.\nTautomerism: A type of isomerism wherein the isomers interchange into one another very early to exist together in equilbrim.\nElectronegativity: Electronegativity is a measure of the tendency of an atom to attract a shared pair of electrons in a covalent bond.\nUltra violet visible spectroscopy: An instrumental scanning method that analyses the absorption of light within UV-Visible region.\nUnsaturated Hydrocarbon: Unsaturated hydrocarbons are hydrocarbons that have double or triple covalent bonds between adjacent carbon atoms.\nVital force theory: A theory that an organic molecule cannot be produced from inorganic molecules, but can only be produced from a living organism or some part of a living organism.\nWilliamson Synthesis: A method of synthesizing ethers by reaction of a sodium alkoxide with a halogen derivative of a hydrocarbon (as an alkyl halide).\navalky aw\n392\nMa\nReferences\nNOT FOR SALE\n1. Shriver and Atkins&#x27; Inorganic Chemistry, Fifth Edition, by P.W. Atkins, T.L. Overton, J.P. Rourke, M.T. Weller, and F.A. Armstrong, Published by W. H. Freeman and Company New York.\n2. General Chemistry: The Essential Concepts, Sixth Edition by R. Chang and J.\nOverby Published by McGraw-Hill,\n3. General chemistry: principles and modern applications, Eleventh edition by Ralph H. Petrucci, F. Geoffrey Herring, Jeffrey D. Madura, Carey Bissonnette. Published by Pearson Canada Inc.\nAdvanced Inorganic chemistry, Third Edition, by F. Albert Cotton and G. Wilkinson Published by John Wiley &amp; Sons, Inc.\n5. Fundamentals of Inorganic chemistry, An introductory text for degree course studies, by J. Barrett and M. A. Malati Published by Horwood Publishing Limited International Publishers Coll House, Westergate, Chichester, West Sussex, PO20 6QL England.\n6.\n7.\n8.\nInorganic Chemistry, by R. Garg and R. Singh, Published by McGraw Hill Education (India) Private Limited.\nOrganic Chemistry by L. G. Wade, Jr. Eight Edition 2013; Pearson Education, Inc.\nOrganic Chemistry by Francis A. Carey; Tenth Edition 2016; McGraw-Hill Higher Education.\n9. Organic Chemistry by David Klein; Third Edition 2017; John Wiley and Sons,\nInc.\n10. Organic Chemistry, by J. Clayden; Second Edition 2012; Oxford University\nPress.\n11. A Textbook of Organic Chemistry by M. Younas; 2017 Edition; Ilmi Kitab\nKhana.\n12. Spectroscopy by D. L. Pavia; Fifth Edition 2015; Cengage Learning.\n13. Organic Spectroscopy and Chromatography by M. Younas: Edition 2007; Ilmi\nKitab Khana.\n¥\n393\nS\nIT\nS\nAuthors&#x27; Profile\nNOT FOR SALE\nJ\nProf. Dr. Khurshid Ali is M.Sc. and M.Phil from Quaid-e-Azam University Islamabad and Ph.D from Middle East Technical University Ankara, Turkey. He has attended many workshops and training sessions on teaching and books writing. He has about 35 years teaching and research experience at Ph.D M.Phil., M.Sc., B.S. and F.Sc. levels. He has produced 23 master, 7 M.Phil, and 6 Ph.D research students. He has translated a book and written chapters in 4 textbooks at inter level. He has also written 55 research papers in journals of international repute with high impact factor. He is also winner of Research Productivity Award from Ministry of Science and Technology, Islamabad.\nDr. Muhammad Ibrahim has been working in the Department of Elementary and Secondary Education Department as Senior Subject Specialist (Chemistry) since 2003. He has obtained his Master degree in Chemistry from University of Peshawar. He got his Ph.D degree in Education from Sarhad University of Science and Information Technology, Peshawar. He has attended a number of seminars and workshops on curriculum and textbook development. He is an author of several articles, which have been published in national and international journals.\nZaid Ullah earned his M.Sc. and M.Phil. degrees from the Institute of Chemical Sciences, University of Peshawar in 2010 and 2014 respectively. He joined the Department of Chemistry, Islamia College Peshawar, as a lecturer in 2011, where he has been teaching both at inter and BS levels. He has extensive experience in teaching and has authored several reference books for intermediate students.\nMushtaq-ur-Rehman is working as Associate Professor in Govt: College, Peshawar. He got his M.Phil Degree in Chemistry from N.C.E in Physical Chemistry from Peshawar University. He has attended numerous seminars and workshops concerning education and development of textbooks.\nMuhammad Amin is working as Principal in Elementary and Secondary Education Department, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa. He got his M.Phil degree in Chemistry. He has attended numerous seminars and workshops regarding Textbook Development. He has also worked as Subject Specialist (Science) in Textbook Board, Peshawar.\n394\nمومن تو آپس میں بھائی بھائی ہیں۔ پس اپنے دو بھائیوں میں صلح کرادیا کرو اور اللہ سے ڈرتے رہو تا کہ تم پر رحمت کی جائے۔\n(سورة الحجرات : ۱۰)\nKhyber Pakhtunkhwa Textbook Board Phase - V, Hayatabad Peshawar\nPhone: 091-9217714-15 Fax: 091-9217163, Website:www.kpb.gov.ple\nTEXTBOOK FEEDBACK FORM\nStatement\nRemarks\n1.\nOverall the book is interesting and user friendly.\nMab\n4.\n5.\n7.\n8.\nThe language and content of the book is age / grade appropriate and the content is free of grammatical and punctuation errors.\nContent is supported with examples from real life/culture. Contents/texts are authentic and updated.\nPictures/diagrams/graphs/illustrations are informative. relevant and clear if not, then identify them.\nActivities, projects and additional work is suggested for reinforcement of concepts.\nAssessment achievements are thought provoking and comprise cognitive, psychomotor and effective skills.\nThe textbook is easy to be covered within academic year.\nPage No.\nGeneral Remarks:\nName &amp; Address:\nContact No. &amp; Email:\nObservation/comments\nSuggested amendment along with rationale\nترانہ",
