        "sciNote": "4. b\n5. d\n6. a\n9. a\n10. d\n1. c\n7. d\nilab.com\nUnit-21\n3.\na\n4. c\n5. d\n6. a\n9.\nb\n10. c\n11. b\n12.\na\n15. c\nUnit-22\n1.\na\n2.\nd\n3. c\n4. c\n5. a\n6. b\n7. c\n8. a\n9. d\n10. c\n11. c\n12. d\n13. b\n14. a\n15. b\nUnit-23\n1. d\n2. d\n3. a\n4. a\n5. d\n6. d\n7. d\n8. a\n9. C\n10. a\n11. b\n12. a\n13. d\n14. a\n15. d\nUnit-24\n1. b\n2. C\n3. a\n4. a\n5. b\n6. a\n7. d\n8. c\n9. a\n10. d\n11. a\n12. d\n13. b\n14. b\n15. d\n385\nK\nNOT FOR SALE\nGLOSSARY\nAlcohols:- Alcohols are organic compounds, in which a hydroxyl group(-OH) is attached to carbon atom of an alkyl group.\nAlkanes:- These are saturated acyclic hydrocarbons which contain all carbon-carbon single bond.\nAlkyl halide:-The organic compounds in which one or more halogen atoms are directly bonded to carbon atom of an alkyl group.\nAlkylation of Ammonia :- The reaction in which hydrogen atoms of NH3 are replaced\nby alkyl groups."
