          "text": "The phenomena of polarization is exactly the same for nitrates and hydrogen carbonates. The small positive ions at the top of the group polarize the nitrate or hydrogen carbonate ions to a greater extent than the larger positive ions at the bottom of the group. Again, the Group – IA compounds need more heat than those in Group – IIA because the Group – IA ions are less polarizing. Thus, thermal stability of anion of Group – I and Group – II increases down the group. The reason is increasing size and decreasing charge density of metal ions.",
