      "content": "<p>Exercise</p><p>Q I. Choose the correct one from the given options.</p><p>1. The carbon of the carbonyl group is</p><p>a. sp³–hybridized.   b. sp²–hybridized.   c. sp–hybridized.   d. dsp²–hybridized.</p><p>2. The reduction of carbonyl to methylene is carried out with</p><p>a. catalytic reduction   b. Metal hydride   c. Clemmensen method   d. Lindlar’s catalyst</p><p>3. Formaldehyde gives an addition product with methyl magnesium iodide which on hydrolysis gives</p><p>a. n–propyl alcohol.   b. isopropyl alcohol.   c. methyl alcohol.   d. ethyl alcohol.</p><p>4. Which of the following compounds can react with ammoniacal silver nitrate solution to form silver mirror?</p><p>a. Acetone   b. Ethanol   c. Dimethyl ether   d. Ethanal</p><p>5. Which of the following compounds will form a precipitate of cupric oxide from Fehling’s reagent but does not react with sodium metal?</p><p>a. C₂H₅OH   b. C₂H₅CHO   c. CH₃CH(OH)CH₃   d. CH₃COCH₃</p><p>6. IUPAC name of acetone is</p><p>a. ethanone.   b. propanone.   c. ethanal.   d. ethanoic acid.</p><p>7. Formalin is</p><p>a. 10% aq. solution of formaldehyde.   b. 20% aq. solution of formaldehyde.   c. 40% aq. solution of formaldehyde.   d. 5% aq. solution of formaldehyde.</p><p>8. An alkene upon ozonolysis gives only one type of aldehyde in product. Identify that alkene.</p><p>a. but–1–ene   b. propene   c. but–2–ene   d. 2,3–dimethylbut–2–ene</p><p>9. Which of the following alkyne would not yield a ketone upon hydration?</p><p>a. acetylene   b. propyne   c. but–1–yne   d. but–2–yne</p>",
