          "text": "Some of the most common organic acids in food are found within fruits. Many people are already aware that citric acid occurs in citrus fruits such as oranges, lemons and limes, but there are lesser known acids in fruits that you may not have heard of. These include malic acid, which is found in apples and tartaric acid found in grapes. These acids provide these fruits with that distinctive sharp taste. The mixture of acid and sugar is what gives fruits their unique flavor, so foods will often be deliberately fermented in particular acids to retain or increase the flavor.",
