      "content": "<p>Exercise</p><p>Q 1. Choose the correct one from the given options.</p><p>1. Which of the following represents the formula of an aromatic carboxylic acids?</p><p>a. HCOOH   b. C₆H₅OH   c. C₆H₅COOH   d. C₆H₅CH₂OH</p><p>2. Which of the following acids is found in rancid butter?</p><p>a. C₂H₄O₂   b. C₃H₆O₂   c. C₄H₈O₂   d. C₅H₁₀O₂</p><p>3. The compound with highest boiling point is</p><p>a. acetic acid.   b. water.   c. ethyl alcohol.   d. diethyl ether.</p><p>4. In which of the following compounds, the carbon atom does not show sp²-hybridization?</p><p>a. Methanal   b. Methanol   c. Methanoic acid   d. Acetone</p><p>5. Which is the strongest acid?</p><p>a. Ethanol   b. Acetic acid   c. Chloroacetic acid   d. Fluoroacetic acid</p><p>6. Acetic acid can be prepared by the hydrolysis of</p><p>a. methyl cyanide.   b. methylmagnescium chloride.   c. ethanal.   d. ethanol.</p><p>7. Fischer esterification is the reaction between</p><p>a. an acid and ester.   b. an acid and alcohol.   c. an acid halide and ester.   d. an ester and sodium hydroxide.</p><p>8. Acyl chloride can be prepared by the reaction of a carboxylic acid with</p><p>a. phosphorous pentoxide.   b. soda lime.   c. hydrochloric acid.   d. thionyl chloride.</p><p>9. The hydrolysis of an ester in presence of alkali is known as</p><p>a. saponification.   b. decarboxylation.   c. esterification.   d. transesterfication.</p><p>10. All the acid derivatives can be converted back into the corresponding acid by one common reaction.</p><p>a. ammonolysis   b. alcoholysis   c. reduction   d. hydrolysis</p>",
