      "content": "<p>The substances, which decrease the activity of an enzyme, known as enzyme inhibitor and this process is known as enzyme inhibition.</p><p>Lipids have three major subclasses: simple lipids, compound lipids and derived lipids.</p><p>The monomer that makes up a nucleic acid is called a nucleotide.</p><p>Nucleotide has three parts: an inorganic phosphate group, a five-carbon monosaccharide sugar, and a nitrogen containing structure known as a nitrogenous base.</p><p>DNA contains genetic information in the form of codes.</p><p>Minerals essential for life are the inorganic nutrients.</p><p>Iron is a part of haemoglobin, a carrier of oxygen in the body.</p><p>Calcium is the main constituent of bones and teeth.</p><p>Living organism cannot synthesized the essential minerals.</p><p>Exercise</p><p>Q I. Choose the correct one from the given options.</p><p>1. The optimum pH of pepsin is around</p><p>a. 3.0   b. 3.5   c. 2.0   d. 2.5</p><p>2. The most abundant carbohydrate found in nature is</p><p>a. cellulose   b. glycogen   c. pectin   d. chitin</p><p>3. The glycosidic linkage is present between the molecules of</p><p>a. glucose   b. glycine   c. fatty acid   d. none of these</p><p>4. Steroid belong to family of</p><p>a. carbohydrates   b. proteins   c. lipids   d. enzymes</p><p>5. Protein present in haemoglobin has the structure known as</p><p>a. primary structure.   b. secondary structure.   c. tertiary structure.   d. quaternary structure.</p><p>6. Which carbohydrate does not conform the general formula Cₙ(H₂O)ₙ?</p><p>a. Deoxyribose   b. Ribose   c. Glucose   d. Fructose</p><p>7. Ethanol is produced from starch by the process of</p><p>a. hydrolysis   b. hydrogenation   c. decomposition   d. fermentation</p><p>8. Human are unable to digest</p><p>a. glucose   b. cellulose   c. starch   d. denatured protein</p><p>9. Which one of the following term is not related to term aldohexose?</p><p>a. Aldehyde   b. Ketone   c. Six   d. Sugar</p><p>10. Slow healing of wounds is due the deficiency of</p><p>a. Ca   b. P   c. Zn   d. Fe</p><p>11. RNA is primarily seen in</p><p>a. nucleus   b. cytoplasm   c. cell wall   d. cell membrane</p><p>12. In which of following disaccharides both the basic structural units are the same?</p><p>a. Maltose   b. Lactose   c. Sucrose   d. All of these</p><p>13. In competitive inhibition, the inhibitor</p><p>a. competes with enzyme.   b. irreversibly binds with the enzyme.   c. binds with substrate.   d. competes with substrate.</p><p>14. In DNA, adenine forms a complementary pair with which other nitrogen base?</p><p>a. Uracil   b. Cytosine   c. Thymine   d. Guanine</p><p>15. Proteins are polymers of</p><p>a. glucose   b. disulphide bridges   c. amino acids   d. peptide bonds</p>",
