      "content": "<p>Exercise</p><p>Q I. Choose the correct one from the given options.</p><p>1. The monomer pair required for the formation of Nylon 6,6 is</p><p>a. hexamethylene diamine + adipic acid.   b. hexamethylene diamine + sebacoyl chloride.   c. hexamethylene diamine + decanoic acid.   d. hexamethylene amine + ethanedioic acid,</p><p>2. Which one is true for DDT?</p><p>a. An antibiotic   b. Non pollutant   c. An antiseptic   d. Non-degradable</p><p>3. The term black gold is used for</p><p>a. coal   b. carbon black   c. petroleum   d. coal tar</p><p>4. All are petrochemicals except</p><p>a. ethylene oxide   b. polypropylene   c. cellulose   d. cyclohexane</p><p>5. Multipart adhesive is an example of</p><p>a. reactive adhesives.   b. contact adhesives.   c. hot adhesives.   d. pressure sensitive adhesives.</p><p>6. Nail polish removers are mainly composed of</p><p>a. propyne   b. propanone   c. propanal   d. propene</p><p>7. In the process of cracking</p><p>a. small molecule unite together.   b. large molecules unite together.   c. large molecules are broken down.   d. small and large molecules unite together.</p><p>8. Rexine is the manipulated form of</p><p>a. plastic (PVC)   b. nylon   c. lipstick   d. nail polish</p><p>9. Identify the petrochemical which is not obtained from benzene</p><p>a. alkyl benzenes   b. cyclohexane   c. nitrobenzene   d. vinyl chloride</p><p>10. Which of the following is condensation polymer</p><p>a. PVC.   b. polythene.   c. nylon.   d. none of these.</p><p>11. (–NH–(CH₂)₆–CONHCO(CH₂)₄CO–)ₙ is an example of</p><p>a. addition polymer.   b. thermosetting polymer.   c. condensation copolymer (Nylon-6,6).   d. homo-polymer.</p><p>12. Which one of the following is synthetic polymer?</p><p>a. cellulose   b. starch   c. silk   d. polythene</p><p>13. Hair dyes are commonly classified into groups</p><p>a. 3   b. 4   c. 5   d. 6</p><p>14. All are synthetic adhesives except</p><p>a. casein glues   b. polyurethanes   c. cyanoacrylates   d. polyimides</p><p>15. Acrylate base polymers are</p><p>a. drying adhesives.   b. pressure sensitive adhesives.   c. contact adhesives.   d. hot adhesives.</p><p>Q2. Write short answers of the following questions.</p><p>i. Differentiate between reactive and non-reactive adhesives.</p><p>ii. How nail-polish remover removes the nail polish?</p><p>iii. Why temporary hair dyes are removed with single shampooing?</p><p>iv. Write down at least four uses of PVC.</p><p>v. What is the difference between petrochemical and chemicals derived from them?</p><p>vi. Differentiate between addition and condensation polymers.</p><p>vii. How would you justify that non-acetone base nail polish remover is better than acetone base nail polish remover.</p><p>viii. How important the safety consideration for the workers in industry?</p><p>ix. What is main goal of petroleum refining?</p><p>Q3. Write detail answers of the following questions.</p><p>1. (a). Explain the Petrochemical Process Technology</p><p>(b). Describe the different types of cracking in detail.</p><p>2. (a). Discuss the preparation and applications of lipsticks.</p><p>(b). Write down in detail the composition of nail polish.</p>",
