          "text": "Flame photometer has both qualitative and quantitative applications. The radiations emitted by the flame photometer are characteristic to particular metal. Flame photometer with monochromators emits radiations of characteristic wavelengths which help to detect the presence of a particular metal in the sample. The concentration of unknown solution can be calculated from working curve of standard solutions. This technique is usually used to find the concentration of various alkali and alkaline earth metals in soil samples which are critical for soil cultivation. Flame photometry is also used to determine the concentrations of Na⁺ and K⁺ ions in biological samples and also estimation of various metals in soft drinks and juices.",
